                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I heavily regret buying the Warfare RPGM bundle. \n\nThese games are the epitome of zero effort RPGM shovelware plaguing Steam. \n\nHope you love getting 1 shot by everything everywhere with all the best gear currently available to you at whatever point of progress you're at. \n\nHope you love grinding job exp in a game where you can't grind in because there are no random encounters and encounters give nothing towards your jobs. \n\nHope you love your job skills not actually being useful because Attack spam is stronger than everything and you're getting one shot by everything anyway. \n\nHope you love having a mage that does more melee damage than your melee jobs equipped with the best melee gear at any point in time and does absolutely no magic damage at all. \n\nHope you love getting softlocked in houses because NPC path mapping is poorly implemented and you can't do anything about it to get NPCs out of the way.\n\nHope you love getting caught on missing obstacles and ending up out of the map everywhere you go. \n\nHope you love reading dialogue cut off from nearly everything the people in the game say.\n\nHope you love aimlessly wandering around the overworld map looking for where to go. Better investigate every single mountain tile because the only dungeons in the game are redesigned mine dungeons and not all of them give you an indication on being accessible. \n\nHope you love getting softlocked on a black screen after the Game Over screen fades away and crashes to desktop because the game wasn't programmed to return to the title screen or save/load screen, so there are no flags being tripped and the game doesn't know what to do but force close.",
